<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 2 December, from 1244 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iv" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1244">1244 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">782 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Innocent IV arrives at Lyon, threatened by Frederick II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Threatened by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iv">Pope Innocent IV</a> arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a>. Early the next year he summoned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> to the First Council of Lyon, at which he excommunicated Frederick and declared him deposed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iv">Pope Innocent IV</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1697">1697 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">329 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wren's new St Paul's Cathedral holds its first service</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The choir of Christopher Wren's new St Paul's opened for worship with a thanksgiving service for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ryswick">Peace of Ryswick</a>. The cathedral, replacing the one lost in the Great Fire, was declared complete in 1711.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1763">1763 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">263 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Touro Synagogue is dedicated in Newport, Rhode Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Jeshuat Israel congregation dedicated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/touro-synagogue">Touro Synagogue</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newport-rhode-island">Newport, Rhode Island</a>, designed by Peter Harrison and built from 1759 under the leadership of Isaac Touro. It is the oldest surviving synagogue building in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/touro-synagogue">Touro Synagogue</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newport-rhode-island">Newport, Rhode Island</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1804">1804 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon crowns himself emperor at Notre-Dame</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the presence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii">Pope Pius VII</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> placed the imperial crown on his own head and then crowned Josephine. The ceremony proclaimed a new hereditary monarchy born of the Revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1805">1805 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">221 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon defeats Austria and Russia at Austerlitz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the first anniversary of his coronation, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> routed a larger Austro-Russian army at Austerlitz in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>. The '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-austerlitz">Battle of the Three Emperors</a>' knocked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> out of the Third Coalition.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1899">1899 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">127 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Filipino rearguard holds Tirad Pass to cover Aguinaldo's escape</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a>, a 60-man Filipino rearguard under Brigadier General Gregorio del Pilar was overcome by more than 500 Americans, but delayed their advance long enough for President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> and his troops to escape.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fermi's team achieves the first controlled nuclear chain reaction</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the stands of Stagg Field at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-chicago">University of Chicago</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enrico-fermi">Enrico Fermi</a>'s team started a self-sustaining chain reaction in Chicago Pile-1. It opened the way to atomic bombs and nuclear power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1971">1971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United Arab Emirates is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>, led by Abu Dhabi and Dubai, formed the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s withdrawal from the Gulf. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> joined in 1972.</p></div></li></ol>
